      "ask": "The primary fraud screening process exits repeatedly with code 15. A restart only buys time, so a person must find the cause of the crash on the primary and fix it before failing back. Fraud screening must stay on, and must not be switched off.; 144 duplicate payments are recorded in the ledger. A person must review and correct them through the bank's own process, since no allowed action may reverse money or edit postings.; The cause of the exit with code 15 is unknown. If the primary exits again, a person must investigate the crash before it is used again."
